WHAT THE POINTERS SAY, which is the second half of the done-when

showBody prints the suspect before and after the installs and the two lines are
IDENTICAL -- same node, same groupBody. So the install does not RE-POINT the
field. It overwrites the CodE inside the one body every reader already shares,
and sets isCodeD on it. The field the install clobbers is Grokking tokenize
itself, in place. That is why a later read tokenizes nothing.

